{
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "Hot: SSD, last 7 days, full replicas \u2014 the <2s search promise lives here",
        "Warm: cheaper disks, fewer replicas, seconds-to-tens-of-seconds search",
        "Cold: object-storage snapshots, restore-to-search, not directly queryable at speed"
      ],
      "title": "Storage tiers"
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "Volume can spike several-fold during an incident \u2014 exactly when search matters most",
        "Kafka absorbs the burst; indexing lags visibly instead of dropping silently",
        "Sampling/drop policy applies to low-value debug logs first, never to errors, and is always counted and alerted"
      ],
      "title": "Incident bursts"
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "items": [
        "2 TB/day x 7 hot days is the expensive core; everything older gets cheaper per GB",
        "ILM rollover, tier migration and deletion are automatic \u2014 retention is a policy, not a hope",
        "Biggest levers: hot retention days, replica count, and not indexing fields nobody searches"
      ],
      "title": "Cost control"
    }
  ],
